# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Hanyu Liu et al. (2026). AI2Pot: A scalable and unified framework for machine-learning interatomic potential development and large-scale molecular dynamic simulations.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2607.06969  arXiv:2607.06969v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2607.06969v2 (sha256 5654aeeba4188eda...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 520 (Software/implementation). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2026ai2pot.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the MTP (level 18) and NEP models trained with
# AI2Pot-cli defaults on a Ge-Sb-Te dataset (2,633 training and 673 test
# frames; crystalline, liquid and amorphous), their training and test
# RMSEs, training times and LAMMPS MD throughput on one GPU. Batch-size
# ratios are figure-only.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
